1. Open PowerShell

Open Windows PowerShell or PowerShell with admin  from the Start menu.

2. Navigate to Your Desktop

Run the following command to change to your Desktop directory:

cd "$HOME\Desktop"

3. Set the Execution Policy

If scripts are blocked, allow locally created scripts to run for your current user:

Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope CurrentUser RemoteSigned

If prompted, enter Y and press Enter.

4. Run a Script

Navigate to the directory containing the script, then run it using .\ followed by the filename.

For example:

.\script.ps1
